{"type": "answer", "run_id": "burst-20261110T183141Z", "scenario": "burst", "source": "stand-in", "setting": "large", "setting_def": {"piece_chars": 2400, "k": 3, "rerank": false, "router": true}, "drafter": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "qid": "Q9", "request_id": "burst-20261110T183141Z-0018", "start_time": "2026-11-10T18:32:05.482+00:00", "arrival_offset_s": 24.244, "patience_s": 69.78, "gave_up": false, "waited_ms": 7081.6, "degraded": true, "reply": {"request_id": "burst-20261110T183141Z-0018", "question": "What makes Moshi full-duplex, and how does it handle both sides speaking at once?", "kind": "answer", "level": 2, "text": "Moreover, Inner Monologue decomposes speech on a per-frame basis, which means that each prediction step outputs a speech frame. [S1]", "sources": [{"sid": "S1", "cite": "2410.00037v1 p.5 §2", "pid": "moshi:2400:0007", "paper": "moshi", "block_ids": ["moshi-p05-b001", "moshi-p05-b002"]}, {"sid": "S2", "cite": "2410.00037v1 pp.6-7 §3.1", "pid": "moshi:2400:0009", "paper": "moshi", "block_ids": ["moshi-p06-b005", "moshi-p07-b001", "moshi-p07-b002"]}], "notice": "shorter answer from fewer passages, without the extra checks, because the service is busy", "eta_s": null, "model_calls": [{"step": "draft", "model": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "status": 200, "outcome": "ok", "prompt_tokens": 963, "completion_tokens": 37}], "spans": [{"name": "plan", "start_ms": 0.0, "end_ms": 0.9, "model": null, "outcome": "lean", "detail": {"predicted_wait_s": {"full": {"openai/gpt-oss-120b": 26.20820229999663, "openai/gpt-oss-20b": 17.591054799995618, "qwen/qwen3.8-27b": 10.649994699997478}, "lean": {"openai/gpt-oss-120b": 22.540702300000703, "openai/gpt-oss-20b": 13.87105480000173, "qwen/qwen3.8-27b": 6.817494699993404}}, "drafter": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b"}}, {"name": "understand", "start_ms": 0.9, "end_ms": 0.9, "model": null, "outcome": "skipped (lean)", "detail": {}}, {"name": "retrieve", "start_ms": 0.9, "end_ms": 1.4, "model": null, "outcome": "1 search", "detail": {"query": "